C0017.description:
`compose()` applies `_apply_phenotype_transform()` to domain and situation packets without checking whether those packets are HARD:
for packet in packets:
    if packet.layer == "domain":
        packet.text = _apply_phenotype_transform(packet.text, transform)
and:
if situation:
    situation.text = _apply_phenotype_transform(situation.text, transform)
    packets.append(situation)
But `_apply_phenotype_transform()` can strip examples, strip rationale, simplify language, compress tables, deduplicate, and truncate:
if len(text) > transform.max_directive_chars:
    text = (
        text[: transform.max_directive_chars].rstrip()
        + "\n[... truncated for model capacity]"
    )
Therefore HARD domain or HARD situation packets can be modified or truncated before coherence pruning and before final rendering.
